so it's not only chris matthews on msnbc  that in his panic about bernie sanders  recent primary and caucus successes  likened bernie to nazis we've actually  been covering the disinformation  propaganda  and the memes that have been spreading  and the american right  is in as much of a panic over bernie  sanders  as is establishment corporate media and  the democratic party establishment and  the right is now starting to spread  disinformation  equating bernie to hitler now i want to  look at one example today  which in six different ways suggests  that  bernie sanders is like adolf hitler  now we have to suspend disbelief for a  moment because  when you say yeah the jewish candidate  whose family members were killed in the  holocaust  by hitler's nazis is like hitler  immediately most people would say that  doesn't make any sense david let's  ignore that for now and just look at  what they assert let's look at these one  by one the meme  claims that both hitler and bernie  believe state power will fix their  respective countries  it's important to point out that bernie  sanders  has no interest in increasing state  power  and in fact bernie has been critical of  how donald trump has exposed that the  executive branch probably has too much  power  because trump has been able to  completely flout and ignore  laws and norms and do whatever the hell  he wants  so it is simply not true that bernie is  looking to increase state power  uh for these hegemonic authoritarian  reasons that hitler wanted to do that  what bernie believes is that government  involvement in a sensible and controlled  way  will make some of our systems better  function there are systems that aren't  working well  that have turned over too much power to  the rich into corporations at the  expense of the average american  bernie believes government involvement  in those systems will be better for the  average person  secondly they argue bernie and hitler  are the same because they both proposed  gun control  now this relates to a meme that has  spread  that the jews were disarmed by nazis  and if the jews had not been disarmed by  nazis and had rifles and handguns  they could have successfully resisted  world war ii  period that has been widely debunked  it's an  entire we could do an hour just on that  but it is both factually wrong and it's  wrong in its conclusions  bernie wants sensible gun control that  most americans agree with  gun control was already strict in  germany  before hitler came to power historians  agree that guns  would not have allowed the jews who made  up just one percent of the german  population at the time  to resist the third reich and the idea  that one percent of the population with  pistols and handguns was going to take  out take out a very well-armed police  state  uh uh that ultimately became and worked  with  and molded into melded into the third  reich is silly at its face and has been  widely debunked  the third bullet point is both hitler  and bernie promise political revolution  now in a sense so did donald trump a  revolution  where the swamp would be drained  political insiders would no longer have  power  he failed to do it but this idea of  revolution  is so vague that it becomes meaningless  hitler's revolution was one of a  hegemonic germany  invading other countries and killing  jews  likening it to bernie sanders wanting  the  the u.s to be more like the social  democracy of denmark  where people get health care and public  college paid for  through taxes is laughable it is a  semantic  game that they are playing number four  they bring out the term  socialist the uh right-wing  disinformation meme says hey hitler  called himself a socialist and bernie  calls himself a socialist now of course  national socialist abbreviated as nazi  has nothing to do whatsoever with  democratic socialism or in reality with  social democracy that's what bernie  sanders  is proposing this is a semantic  confusion that's being used to trick low  information people  who don't really know much by throwing  the word socialism in without any  context  number five hitler blamed jews for  germany's problems while bernie blames  the rich for america's problems  this is a really important one bernie is  not so much blaming the rich  for problems now even if bernie was  blaming the rich  blaming the rich is very different than  blaming the jews but put that aside for  a second  bernie doesn't blame the rich bernie  points to the super rich  as evidence that the system is not  working and needs to be reformed when  bernie says look at  the super rich in corporations who often  pay little  or less in taxes compared to people who  are just middle class  that's evidence that the system isn't  working the richer a side effect  the rich aren't the problem as  individuals  a very very deceptive component and then  lastly  both uh hitler and bernie wanted heavily  regulated economies and again this is  just a semantic game  a regulated economy could mean anything  from a communist centrally planned  economy  to social democracy or even a  totalitarian police state hitler wanted  to get involved  in the minutia of people's everyday  lives in the authoritarian sense  determine who gets to live who gets to  procreate  bernie wants to regulate the economy to  prevent bad actors in industry  and uh bad actors who limit the average  person's ability to just live a happy  life and pursue happiness  so this is one of those examples where  you see the full list with the deceptive  language and you start to think man  maybe bernie is like hitler in some ways  the merest superficial analysis confirms  that this is merely disinformation  and uh something that we need to protect  ourselves against  given the nature of the nature  and the scope of the disinformation that  is floating around already in the  democratic primary  very very ugly stuff but we will do our  best to debunk it  if you watch the david pakman show you  